(3551525, 494260, 59148, '<td valign="top">After reading your post and finally getting to see the photo your refering to in your post I see the issue people are having. Idea is great composition is good motion blurr good but photo lacks a focus point. I would have gave this a 4 for the lack there of. If you would have had the two dominoes not falling in focus it would have been a 7 or 8. Hope this helps</td>', 'After reading your post and finally getting to see the photo your refering to in your post I see the issue people are having. Idea is great composition is good motion blurr good but photo lacks a focus point. I would have gave this a 4 for the lack there of. If you would have had the two dominoes not falling in focus it would have been a 7 or 8. Hope this helps', '2007-04-16 10:21:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(3551544, 494533, 57378, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by craigester:</b></div><hr/><i> Well done on the finish for this. AS this was Advanced Editing, why didn''t you simply clone out the thingy sticking out of the chain? I think you may have got a top 5 if you had... I do also agree with other comments that the girl is a bit small in this composition and this could possibly have hurt you here. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I was wondering what I could get away with - When I read the rules though <br/> <br/>clone out incidental power lines, twigs, dust specks, stray hairs, and similar minor imperfections.<br/> <br/>I thought it was a little more than a power line etc - Any thoughts from anyoneas ti if I would have gotten away with getting rid of the thing above the chain?<br/>JEff</td>', 'Originally posted by craigester: Well done on the finish for this. AS this was Advanced Editing, why didn''t you simply clone out the thingy sticking out of the chain? I think you may have got a top 5 if you had... I do also agree with other comments that the girl is a bit small in this composition and this could possibly have hurt you here.   I was wondering what I could get away with - When I read the rules though  clone out incidental power lines, twigs, dust specks, stray hairs, and similar minor imperfections. I thought it was a little more than a power line etc - Any thoughts from anyoneas ti if I would have gotten away with getting rid of the thing above the chain?JEff', '2007-04-16 10:25:50.000000', NULL, 0),
