(3558923, 493699, 15291, '<td valign="top">Morning Ja,<br/>          Very nice &amp; interesting image. The shadow coming down his right side is a little disconcearning. His leg (closest to window) is a wee bit to dark for me. That being said wonderful image.</td>', 'Morning Ja,          Very nice & interesting image. The shadow coming down his right side is a little disconcearning. His leg (closest to window) is a wee bit to dark for me. That being said wonderful image.', '2007-04-18 11:12:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(3558927, 494492, 62787, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club.<br/> <br/>I gave this image a 4 during voting. It''s not that there''s any one thing specifically wrong with the image per se... It''s just a bit dull. Taking a picture of a chain for the ''chains'' challenge is the most literal interpretation you can think of, the title is unimaginative, and it''s not a very pretty chain either.<br/> <br/>From a technical point of view, the photo is fine - shooting in RAW did work, the bokeh works well, the small bits of railing cut off on the right actually frame the image quite nicely.<br/> <br/>The background colour is complementary, but boring, the fact that the chain is rusty makes it less aesthetically pleasing, but is insufficient to make it interesting.<br/> <br/>Looking at the other photos in your portfolio, you have the technical skill, the imagination, and the aesthetic sense to capture things that are genuinely beautiful and unique. Please use those. This image doesn''t do you justice at all.<br/> <br/>Jelena</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club. I gave this image a 4 during voting. It''s not that there''s any one thing specifically wrong with the image per se... It''s just a bit dull. Taking a picture of a chain for the ''chains'' challenge is the most literal interpretation you can think of, the title is unimaginative, and it''s not a very pretty chain either. From a technical point of view, the photo is fine - shooting in RAW did work, the bokeh works well, the small bits of railing cut off on the right actually frame the image quite nicely. The background colour is complementary, but boring, the fact that the chain is rusty makes it less aesthetically pleasing, but is insufficient to make it interesting. Looking at the other photos in your portfolio, you have the technical skill, the imagination, and the aesthetic sense to capture things that are genuinely beautiful and unique. Please use those. This image doesn''t do you justice at all. Jelena', '2007-04-18 11:13:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(3558945, 494079, 15291, '<td valign="top">Morning hajeka,<br/> <br/>              What else can I say, you nailed it. Comp, texture, tonality &amp; creative. Wonderful image.</td>', 'Morning hajeka,               What else can I say, you nailed it. Comp, texture, tonality & creative. Wonderful image.', '2007-04-18 11:16:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(3558965, 494458, 71092, '<td valign="top">The Star of India... Ahhh San Diego Bay. Love it.</td>', 'The Star of India... Ahhh San Diego Bay. Love it.', '2007-04-18 11:19:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(3559042, 494691, 15291, '<td valign="top">Morning Coley,<br/>             Nice image. The comp is well done &amp; your toneal rangers are excellent. Two things here do need addressing. His right hand seems a bit washed by refection of light, &amp; there is something missing. Mood or expression just seems image is to clean.</td>', 'Morning Coley,             Nice image. The comp is well done & your toneal rangers are excellent. Two things here do need addressing. His right hand seems a bit washed by refection of light, & there is something missing. Mood or expression just seems image is to clean.', '2007-04-18 11:33:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(3559076, 494759, 15291, '<td valign="top">Morning pipersd,<br/>               I do not like he compostion here. To busy, my eye wonders all over the place. The white rope, the boat, the post &amp; chain. There is way to much cloud seen here, cropping just above the boats mast would have been just right. The water also has been burned to much (obvious). Perhaps a different angle or possibly depth of field blurring the boat would have helped here.<br/></td>', 'Morning pipersd,               I do not like he compostion here. To busy, my eye wonders all over the place. The white rope, the boat, the post & chain. There is way to much cloud seen here, cropping just above the boats mast would have been just right. The water also has been burned to much (obvious). Perhaps a different angle or possibly depth of field blurring the boat would have helped here.', '2007-04-18 11:45:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(3559112, 494550, 15291, '<td valign="top">Morning flash,<br/>             Funny &amp; creative. The only problem for me here is the visual effect used here, it makes the whole image look out of focus.</td>', 'Morning flash,             Funny & creative. The only problem for me here is the visual effect used here, it makes the whole image look out of focus.', '2007-04-18 11:52:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(3559349, 494688, 62787, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club. <br/> <br/>I gave this image a 6 during voting, which should actually be seriously flattering - I was downmarking pretty much all just chains images on the basis of lack of originality, and the ones that had matching titles like ''chains'' or ''linked'' were particularly grating on me, on the basis of both lack of originality and absence of imagination... Therefore it''s a sort of miracle of life that this one got over 5 from me.<br/> <br/>What I think really makes it work is the simplicity of the composition - there''s something very graceful about the minimalism of it. And it''s got that lovely curved diagonal shape that a number of your images seem to have, which really works for me, I find it very elegant. The bokeh works very well, and the background is good - the shadows are interesting, but without distracting from the main subject. The light is nice, the texture is good. <br/> <br/>It''s quite sharp, but probably not as sharp as it could be. Also, I find it slightly too close up - I would have liked to see the same curve, but from slightly further off, so that more of the links in the chain are shown.<br/> <br/>So yeah, overall a nice image, but I do wish the subject matter was more original.<br/> <br/>Jelena</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club.  I gave this image a 6 during voting, which should actually be seriously flattering - I was downmarking pretty much all just chains images on the basis of lack of originality, and the ones that had matching titles like ''chains'' or ''linked'' were particularly grating on me, on the basis of both lack of originality and absence of imagination... Therefore it''s a sort of miracle of life that this one got over 5 from me. What I think really makes it work is the simplicity of the composition - there''s something very graceful about the minimalism of it. And it''s got that lovely curved diagonal shape that a number of your images seem to have, which really works for me, I find it very elegant. The bokeh works very well, and the background is good - the shadows are interesting, but without distracting from the main subject. The light is nice, the texture is good.  It''s quite sharp, but probably not as sharp as it could be. Also, I find it slightly too close up - I would have liked to see the same curve, but from slightly further off, so that more of the links in the chain are shown. So yeah, overall a nice image, but I do wish the subject matter was more original. Jelena', '2007-04-18 12:50:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(3559391, 494213, 75781, '<td valign="top">Thanks!! At least someone got it!</td>', 'Thanks!! At least someone got it!', '2007-04-18 13:00:27.000000', NULL, 0),
